sara-customer: Hey team — our production chatflow started throwing JSON parse errors this morning after a Redwood API call in JSON mode. ~200 requests failing per minute. Error from our side: "Unexpected token t in JSON at position 0". Not seeing any obvious changes on our end. Can someone help?

alex_support: Sorry to hear that — can you paste the exact model response you got (the raw body)? Also which model + params (temperature, max_tokens) are you using?

sara-customer: Pasting redacted output + curl we used:

sara-customer: ```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate 
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk-REDACTED' 
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' 
  -d '{
    "model":"redwood-structured-1",
    "mode":"json",
    "prompt":"GENERATE_JSON_V1...",
    "temperature":0.0,
    "max_tokens":256
  }'

# response body:
{
  "result": {
    "id": "abc-123",
    "summary": "Fixed the issue, see notes below"
  }
}
Note: our parser sees the first char as 't' — our logs show something like:
  t
  {"result":...
Which suggests there's a stray 't' before the JSON object.
```

maria_cs: Thanks for the example. We're flagging this P1 and looping in runtime + ML. Apologies for the customer impact. We'll post updates here.

jon-eng-runtime: Looking. Can you also share the full raw bytes (base64 ok) or exact Content-Length/encoding? Is this happening on streaming endpoints or single-response?

sara-customer: Non-streaming endpoint. Content-Length 482. We attached a zipped sample to the support ticket (ticket# 2024-0379).

li-ml: Quick hypothesis: model might be emitting a short stray token (e.g., 't' or commentary) before the JSON object. In JSON mode we enforce deterministic sampling, but decoding artifacts can still lead to prefix text. Can you confirm system prompt + any user-supplied instruction that might cause commentary?

alex_support: Temporary workaround for production: implement a tolerant parser that strips leading non-{ characters and attempts to find the first '{' or '[' and parse from there. We can share a small snippet for Node/Python. Also set max_tokens slightly higher to avoid truncation mid-JSON.

maria_cs: Communicating to customer: we're suggesting a short mitigation + we'll deliver a server-side sanitizer in a few hours.\\n
deploy-bot: deploy started: json-sanitizer-hotfix -> canary (job# 89523)

jon-eng-runtime: Root cause: in some cases when response is near token limit the tokenizer emits a short partial token (single letter) before the JSON object due to decoder resync after stopping token generation. We're pushing a hotfix that post-processes model output to trim stray prefixed characters and validate JSON before returning to customers.

li-ml: Follow ups: add unit tests for JSON mode that inject random prefix tokens and ensure sanitizer recovers valid JSON or fails gracefully with clear error. Also evaluate switching to function-calling response mode for structured outputs — function mode guarantees strict schema emission from the model side.

alex_support: Action items for customer: 1) temporary client patch (safe_json_parse) to extract first JSON object (we'll paste code below), 2) set max_tokens +20 for now, 3) if you can switch to function-calling / tool calling for critical flows that require strict parsing, that avoids this class of failure.

alex_support: Node snippet:```
function safeJsonParse(s) {
  const start = s.indexOf('{');
  if (start === -1) throw new Error('no-json-found');
  const trimmed = s.slice(start);
  try { return JSON.parse(trimmed); } catch (e) {
    // fallback heuristic: try to find matching closing brace by scanning
    let depth=0; let end=-1;
    for (let i=0;i<trimmed.length;i++){
      if (trimmed[i]=='{') depth++;
      if (trimmed[i]=='}') depth--;
      if (depth==0){ end=i+1; break; }
    }
    if (end==-1) throw e;
    return JSON.parse(trimmed.slice(0,end));
  }
}
```

maria_cs: Notifying customer now with the mitigation steps + ETA for server-side fix (ETA ~4 hours). We'll offer a credit for incident impact if this persists.

sara-customer: Thanks — applying client patch now. Please confirm once hotfix is fully rolled to prod.

jon-eng-runtime: Hotfix is live in canary, results look good on smoke tests. Rolling to 20% -> 100% in next 3 hours, will update here when at 100%.

maria_cs: We updated the ticket with the patch, steps, and credit offer. Customer appreciated the quick response.

alex_support: Postmortem followups: create a KB entry on "JSON mode parse failures" with recommended SDK helper, prompt templates, and guidance to use function-calling for strict schemas.

li-ml: Long term: change decoding constraints for structured mode to prevent stray prefix tokens + add metrics that count "sanitizer corrections" so we can detect regressions.

jon-eng-runtime: Marking thread resolved pending customer confirmation. If you still see failures after SDK patch + hotfix, please reopen ticket 2024-0379.

sara-customer: Confirmed — after applying safeJsonParse all past errors stopped. Thanks everyone for the fast turnaround :thumbsup:
